    "headline": "THE STANDINGS AND THE NUMBERS HAVE STOPPED AGREEING",
    "deck": "California is 5-1 with a losing all-play record. Off Boys is 3-3 with the third-best all-play mark. Week 6 did not clarify the league. It exposed the fault lines.",
    "story": [
      "Redwood Murder and California Un-Named Team share the league\u2019s best record at 5-1, but they arrived there by very different statistical roads. Redwood owns a 35-31 all-play mark. California is 32-34, meaning its weekly scores would have lost more often than won against the full league field despite five head-to-head victories.",
      "The strongest underlying profiles belong to Turbulent Ticklesh!ts and Sullco MethMouths. They rank first and second in both total points and all-play performance, yet both trail the 5-1 leaders at 4-2. Their records are good. Their weekly strength has been even better.",
      "No team has a larger standings-to-performance disconnect than Off Boys. At 3-3, Off Boys sits seventh in the official league order, but ranks third in points scored and third in all-play at 44-22. The record says bubble team. The full-season scoring says contender.",
      "Week 6 itself was a contradiction. THE Barton Spartans led the league with only 114.10 points, California won a 66.92-64.12 grinder, and Your Mom escaped Space Cadets by 1.78. Low scoring compressed the field and made every lineup failure more expensive."
    ],
